🛠️ Crafting Recipes & Field Manual
To operate the Type 11 LMG, you will need to manufacture both the weapon itself and the specialized 6.5x50mm ammunition.
1. The Single Round
Craft the individual bullets first. This recipe yields a single Type 11 Round.
Top Row: Empty | Iron Nugget | Empty
Middle Row: Copper Ingot | Gunpowder | Copper Ingot
Bottom Row: Empty | Redstone Dust | Empty
2. The 5-Round Clip (Ammo)
The Type 11 utilizes a hopper-feed system that strips rounds from 5-round clips. This is a shapeless recipe—simply place 5 individual rounds anywhere in the crafting grid.
Requirements: 5x Type 11 Round
Result: 1x Type 11 Ammo (Clip)
3. The Type 11 Light Machine Gun
To bypass vanilla crafting limits while maintaining the heavy iron cost of a true machine gun, you will need to forge Iron Blocks for the receiver.
Top Row: Iron Ingot | Iron Block | Iron Block
Middle Row: Wooden Plank (Any) | Gold Ingot | Iron Ingot
Bottom Row: Empty | Iron Ingot | Empty
Result: 1x Type 11 Weapon
⚠️ OPERATOR WARNING: This weapon does not feature a safety mechanism. It fires from an open bolt. Keep your finger off the trigger when standing near pets, villagers, or valuable redstone machinery.

